<properties>
{"title":"Performance Standards"}
</properties>
<content>
<callout icon="📌" color="gray_bg">
	These are not suggestions — they are the standard. Hit these benchmarks consistently and you have a place here long-term. Miss them and we coach you. Keep missing them and we replace you.
</callout>
---
## 📊 Setter Benchmarks
- Booking rate: 70%+ (triage contacts to booked calls)
- No-show rate: Under 20% on booked calls
- Speed-to-contact: Under 5 minutes from application to first call attempt
- CRM note quality: Every booked lead has structured, detailed notes — not one-liners
- EOD submissions: 100% every single day you work
---
## 🎯 Closer Benchmarks
- Close rate: 40%+ (calls taken to closed deals)
- No-close follow-up rate: 100% — every no-close gets a follow-up sequence started same day
- Post-call notes: Submitted within 30 minutes of every call, closed or not
- CRM updated: Immediately after every call — no exceptions
- EOD submissions: 100% every single day you work
---
## 📅 Weekly Review Schedule
- Every Friday: Submit weekly metrics via EOD form
- Every Monday: AM huddle — time TBD (being scheduled as the team is structured; announced in Slack 1-general) — mandatory
- Monthly: Strategy call with management — metrics review + coaching
---
## ⚠️ Underperformance Protocol
- First instance: Coaching call within 48 hours + 2-week improvement window
- Second instance: Final warning + written performance improvement plan
- Third instance: Removed from the team
---
## 🚨 Immediate Removal — No Warning Window
<callout icon="🚫" color="red_bg">
	Missing EODs consistently without notice<br>Not updating CRM after calls<br>Ghosting leads after they've booked<br>Lying about metrics or call outcomes<br>Disrespecting leads or creating legal liability
</callout>
*We celebrate wins loudly and address problems directly. If you're struggling, speak up — we coach people who want to improve. We remove people who stop caring.*
</content>
</page>
